00:15:59.840 --> 00:16:14.970
<v Jim Trainum>And one of the things that we knew about was at the homeless shelter where she was living at the time, there was this log where you could sign and in sign out. And so I got a subpoena, went to the homeless shelter, and got the log.
<v Jim Trainum>我们知道的一件事是，在她当时居住的无家可归者收容所里，有一本记录本，你可以签入和签出。所以我申请了传票，去了收容所，拿到了那本记录。

00:16:14.970 --> 00:16:35.720
<v Jim Trainum>And I was bringing it back to the office, and I flipped to the pages that had the entries for the night of the murder. And I looked down, and I about wrecked the car. She wasn't out during the critical times that we needed her out. And in fact, according to that book, there was no way that she could have participated in the murder.
<v Jim Trainum>我把它带回办公室，翻到谋杀案当晚的记录页。我往下看了一眼，差点把车撞了。她在我们需要的关键时刻并没有外出。事实上，根据那本书，她根本不可能参与谋杀。

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:39.040
<v Saul Elbein>And this is not like, OK, wait, stop?
